  <title>Conversation Area</title>
  <p>The native GTK conversation area displays the conversation of the selected agent, including assistant responses, reasoning, notices, tool activity, and turn summaries in selectable components and visible step frames.</p>
  <p>Assistant responses are handled as Markdown through the direct libcmark-gfm path. GitHub Flavored Markdown tables are rendered as native tables, and inline `$...$`/`\(...\)` and standalone `$$...$$`/`\[...\]` math use the
native Ada engine for supported common constructs, including fractions,
scripts, roots, arrays, font styles, delimiters, limits, and selected accents
(such as dot accents). Code is
protected; unsupported and legacy MathML-shaped source remains visible as text.
This is not full TeX or complete KaTeX compatibility. Streaming text may remain plain until the completed response block is rendered.</p>
  <p>Math is processed in the background after a response block completes. Its
source remains visible while processing is pending or if a formula cannot be
rendered. Copying rendered inline math restores its original delimited source.</p>
  <p>For a display formula, expand <gui>Math structure</gui> to inspect a
keyboard-navigable tree of mathematical parts and source positions. The tree
fills incrementally; this view does not imply complete screen-reader support
or KaTeX compatibility.</p>
  <p>In the GTK conversation, local images in assistant Markdown can be shown when their files are within the active session directory. Alt text stays visible beside the image for selection, copying, and search. Remote images are not fetched; unavailable or unsupported images appear as alt text. Plain output, SQC replay, and images in table cells remain text-only.</p>
  <p>The <gui>Agents Window</gui> support window treats each agent as a virtual window. Selecting a live row changes the conversation shown in the main window and puts that agent in the driver's seat for prompts and applicable controls. Selecting a completed row shows its retained conversation for review. Hiding the support window does not stop agents or discard the tree.</p>
  <p>Select text to publish it through the desktop PRIMARY selection. Copy, Select All, and Deselect All operate on the focused conversation component, or on a retained conversation selection when no conversation text view has focus. Prompt focus keeps these commands on the prompt. Completed tool cards and fork controls can be activated with the mouse or keyboard.</p>
  <p>When a conversation text view has focus, use <key>j</key>/<key>k</key> for line movement, <key>g</key> for the top, <key>G</key> or Shift+<key>g</key> for the bottom, and Ctrl+<key>D</key>/Ctrl+<key>U</key> for page movement. Prompt, agent-tree, and list controls retain their native keyboard behavior.</p>
  <p>Use a tool card’s <gui>View Details</gui> action to open an independent snapshot inspector. Metadata and the Close and Help actions stay visible. Arguments and Result scroll separately; drag the horizontal divider to give either pane more space. Long metadata values have full-value tooltips and remain selectable and copyable. The Edit menu operates on the focused text area or metadata value. A snapshot opened while a call is running does not update: reopen View Details after completion to see the result.</p>
  <p>See <link xref="keyboard-shortcuts">Keys &amp; Shortcuts</link> for navigation and selection commands.</p>
</page>
